# Test creation

When the user asks to create tests, use the matching project skill and obey path rules under `.cursor/rules/`:

| Request | Skill | Rules |
| ------- | ----- | ----- |
| Manual / QA checklist | `manual-test-cases` | `manual-test-cases.mdc` |
| API / endpoint / cy.request | `api-test-author` | `api-tests.mdc` |
| E2E / browser flow | `e2e-test-author` | `e2e-tests.mdc` |
| Page object / POM | `page-object-author` | `page-objects.mdc` |
| Stubbed UI / Jest page test | `stubbed-ui-test-author` | `stubbed-ui-tests.mdc` |

Shared detail: `.cursor/skills/_shared/marlow-test-conventions.md`.

API and e2e skills write **both Cypress and Playwright** unless the user names one framework.

## Manual → automation handoff

When the user says a manual case is **done**, **complete**, **ready to automate**, or asks to **write API/e2e/stubbed tests from** a `docs/test-cases/*.md` file:

1. Read that markdown file.
2. Split cases by layer:
   - **API** — HTTP status/body (login, list orders empty, etc.) → follow `api-test-author`
   - **E2E** — browser navigation, redirects, visible empty states → follow `e2e-test-author`
   - **Stubbed UI** — component empty/loading/error with mocked API → follow `stubbed-ui-test-author`
3. Skip or note cases that are exploratory-only / not automatable.
4. Prefer extending shared `fixtures/` for API; keep Cypress and Playwright in sync.
